  "rationale": "R1, data-informed (not zero-shot): the numbers of flex_heptane.wsp2 D2, unchanged, with one number added: the probability (one in ten) that the radiative clock of an atmosphere is not the law's, in which case it keeps the law's median and has a very wide spread. The third-generation law gives a flame that is burning long after its clock a probability of 1e-8, which no measurement in a prefix can move; the train run that showed it (n-heptane at 2 atm in CO2) was found when the flame cameras were read. The number is not read off the train runs, where the law is right by construction and the number can only cost: it is the author's expectation of how often a law typed from two dozen atmospheres is far off in a new one. The flame cameras are switched off. No fit, no search; no validation outcome was read.",
